            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Sorry, no. By design, 'mini.pairs' works only on with two-character pairs (like `()`, `{}`, etc.) and can be conditioned only by two-character neighborhood (with `neigh_pattern`). This functionality is more suited for snippets.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Sorry, no. By design, 'mini.pairs' works only on with two-character pairs (like <code class=\"notranslate\">()</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">{}</code>, etc.) and can be conditioned only by two-character neighborhood (with <code class=\"notranslate\">neigh_pattern</code>). This functionality is more suited for snippets.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Sorry, no. By design, 'mini.pairs' works only on with two-character pairs (like (), {}, etc.) and can be conditioned only by two-character neighborhood (with neigh_pattern). This functionality is more suited for snippets.",
